{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\":\"def classify_http_error(status_code: int) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Classify an HTTP status code into an error category.\\n\\n    Expected categories:\\n        - \\\"client_error\\\"  for 400-499\\n        - \\\"server_error\\\"  for 500-599\\n        - \\\"unknown\\\"       for anything else\\n\\n    BUG_59: the implementation lumps ALL codes 400-599 into \\\"server_error\\\"\\n    instead of splitting 4xx (client) from 5xx (server).  Models must\\n    also emit an \\\"error.mapped\\\" metric via orgops.metrics.emit().\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    category: str\\n    if 400 <= status_code < 500:\\n        category = \\\"client_error\\\"\\n    elif 500 <= status_code < 600:\\n        category = \\\"server_error\\\"\\n    else:\\n        category = \\\"unknown\\\"\\n\\n    from orgops.metrics import emit\\n\\n    emit(\\n        \\\"error.mapped\\\",\\n        {\\n            \\\"status_code\\\": status_code,\\n            \\\"category\\\": category,\\n        },\\n    )\\n    return category\\n\",\"comments\":\"Split client vs. server status ranges and fire the error.mapped metric for each classification.\"}"}}
